-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",198,{
[6305]="70041A50\n1\tMeet Jajax at Hata Kebir\tHata Kebir can be found due east of Aerthir in south-eastern Lebennin. Jajax has asked you to aid him in fighting against the Heirs of Castamir at Hata Kebir.\n2\tAid Jajax in weakening the leaders of Hata Kebir\030Aid Jajax in stealing his fellow Corsairs' pillage\030Aid Jajax in crippling the forces of Hata Kebir\tHata Kebir can be found in south-eastern Lebennin. Jajax has asked your aid in weakening the forces of the Heirs of Castamir in Hata Kebir.\n3\tAid Jajax in searching Hata Kebir\tJajax can be found at your side or called with your horn. You should aid Jajax in his search of Hata Kebir.\n4\tListen to the tale of Daxamat's journey with Balakhôr the Scourge\tDaxamat can be found in the northernmost area of Hata Kebir in south-eastern Lebennin. You should listen to Daxamat as he recounts the story of his journey to Lebennin alongside the Scourge.\n5\tTalk to Jajax\tJajax can be found at your side or can be called with your horn. You have listened to Daxamat's retelling and should now speak to Jajax.\n6\tTalk to Erchar in Linhir\tErchar can be found in Linhir along the Gilrain in western Lebennin. Jajax has decided to remain with his brother until you are able to rally the forces of Erchar and Herion against the Heirs of Castamir. You should return to Linhir.\n",
[6306]="70059818\n1\tDestroy poisoned traps (total: 10)\tPoisoned traps can be found in the central Wildwood. Linnet has asked you to destroy any poisoned traps that you come across.\n2\tReturn to Linnet\tLinnet can be found in the south-central Wildwood. You should return to Linnet.\n",
[6307]="70057E5F\n1\tHealers can be found in the Houses of Healing on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith. Deliver the letters to the healers.\t\n2\tReturn to the Postmaster\tThe Postmaster is in the House of Craft on the Third Circle of Minas Tirith. You should let the Postmaster know that you have delivered all of the letters.\n",
[6308]="700583F4\n1\tBurn the deceased members of the scouting party\tShakal-atrâd can be found in central Elderslade. You should find what remains of the scouting party and honour their sacrifice.\n2\tBurn the deceased members of the scouting party (total: 8)\030Collect keepsakes from the members of the scouting party (total: 8)\tShakal-atrâd can be found in central Elderslade. You should find what remains of the scouting party and honour their sacrifice.\n3\tReturn to Lóssi with the keepsakes\tLóssi can be found at Annâk-khurfu. You should return to Lóssi with the keepsakes.\n",
[6309]="700265AE\n1\tCollect strongboxes (total: 6)\tStrongboxes full of relics are outside the gates of the tombs of Annúminas on Tyl Annûn.\n2\tBring the strongboxes to Orchalwë\tOrchalwë will want to hold onto the strongboxes until he can return them to Tinnudir.\n",
[6310]="7002EF10\n1\tBurn Rohirrim corpses\t\n2\tBurn Rohirrim corpses (total: 10)\tThere are dead Rohirrim throughout Thornhope. Unable to bury the dead Rohirrim, due to the presence of the Orcs, you should burn the corpses to prevent their further defilement.\n3\tTalk to Béortnoth\tThane Béortnoth is encamped beyond the walls of Thornhope. You should speak with Thane Béortnoth and let him know what you have done.\n",
[6311]="70015E32\n1\tDefeat Shatogtar\030Collect statues (total: 8)\tThere are memorial statues spread all throughout Barad Morlas, south-west of Echad Eregion. Ladenthir has asked you to preserve the memory of the Elves of Eregion by collecting the memorial statues placed in Barad Morlas by the Elves of Rivendell before the half-orcs can despoil them. He also bade you defeat Shatogtar, one of the Uruk-hai.\n2\tBring the statues to Ladenthir at Echad Eregion\tLadenthir is at Echad Eregion, north-east of Barad Morlas. You should return to Ladenthir with tidings of your success.\n",
[6312]="7002D34C\n1\tPlant a banner at the grave of the fallen dwarves\tOutside of the Hollin Gate lies a small graveyard where the fallen dwarves lie. You should plant a banner at the graveyard just outside the Hollin Gate.\n2\tReturn to Ráthulf\tRáthulf is at Durin's Threshold in Moria. You should return to Ráthulf and tell him of your service to the fallen dwarves.\n",
[6313]="70041860\n1\tCollect hand-woven baskets in Malbarth (total: 3)\030Collect fine cloth in Malbarth (total: 3)\030Collect reeds from the banks of the Gilrain (total: 3)\tBaskets and cloth can be found in Malbarth, and reeds can be found along the banks of the Gilrain. Arvaeth has asked for your help in crafting the traditional tribute baskets woven by the people of Lebennin.\n2\tDeliver the baskets and materials to Arvaeth\tArvaeth can be found on the banks of the Gilrain, to the north-west of Malbarth. You have gathered all of the materials Arvaeth asked for and should now return to him with them.\n",
[6314]="7000F492\n1\tTalk to Garbert\tGarbert is at his cottage in Tâl Bruinen, south and west of Rivendell. Haldúr has asked that you visit Garbert and purchase fishing supplies from him because of his injuries.\n",
[6315]="7002FCFD\n1\tPlant new crops at the crofts of Garsfeld (total: 8)\tBernwyn wants you to plant new crops in any remaining viable soil outside of Garsfeld. Plots can be found in all surrounding fields of Garsfeld.\n2\tTalk to Bernwyn\tYou have planted numerous crops where the soil remained fertile enough to do so. You should return to Bernwyn in Garsfeld.\n",
[6316]="7002FECB\n1\tTalk to Hubyrt\tThe crofters and guard-captain are in Walstow centre. Winsig is worried that her crofters are losing hope and wants you to speak with them about their concerns. After that, she would like to hear a report.\n2\tComfort Hubyrt with a hug, calming words, a mighty flex, or a story\tHubyrt is standing in Walstow. You should try to comfort him with a hug, some calming words, a mighty flex, or an enthralling story.\n3\tTalk to Adalgifu\tAdalgifu is standing in central Walstow. Winsig is worried that her crofters are losing hope and wants you to speak with them about their concerns. After that, she would like to hear a report.\n4\tComfort Adalgifu with a hug, calming words, a mighty flex, or a story\tAdalgifu is in Walstow. You should try to comfort her with a hug, some calming words, a mighty flex, or an enthralling story.\n5\tTalk to Egelferth\tThe Rohirrim guard-captain, Egelferth, is stationed at the north end of Walstow. Winsig is worried that her crofters are losing hope and wants you to speak with them about their concerns. After that, she would like to hear a report.\n6\tSalute Egelferth before returning to Winsig\tThe guard-captain is in Walstow. You should give the guard-captain a salute.\n7\tTalk to Winsig\tWinsig can be found in the Mead Hall of Walstow.\n",
[6317]="70015267\n1\tLight the cauldrons (total: 6)\tThe cauldrons are to the east in Jundul-dûm. Borgar has asked you to light several cauldrons along the road leading east from Jazârgund.\n2\tTalk to Borgar at Jazârgund\tBorgar is at Jazârgund, west of Jundul-dûm. Borgar will be pleased to hear that the reinforcements he requested will now be able to find their way.\n",
[6318]="70028265\n1\tTalk to Naeglanc at Echad Naeglanc\tNaeglanc is at Echad Naeglanc, west of the cairns where Mair is posted. Mair has asked you to speak with Naeglanc regarding the remnants of the vessel you recovered.\n2\tTalk to Lhucu at her hut\tLhucu's hut sits upon a ridge west of Echad Naeglanc, between Lhan Gogledh and Lhan Bach. Naeglanc suggested that you speak with Lhucu, daughter of Trehéarn Brenin, regarding the urn.\n",
[6319]="7002EE55\n1\tTalk to Thane Wulfrad at Thornhope\tThane Wulfrad is at Thornhope, north-west of Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale. Reeve Ingbert asked you to go to Thane Wulfrad and learn the circumstances of Thornhope that prevented them from sending aid to Eaworth.\n",
[6320]="700346E1\n1\tHarvested crops can be found throughout Dunfast near many of the buildings. You should check the crops for spoilage, and gather any that are still safe to eat.\t\n2\tBring the crops you salvaged to Gifemund\tGifemund can be found at the refugees' encampment south-west of Dunfast. You should bring the crops you rescued to Gifemund.\n",
[6321]="7002EF48\n1\tCollect Orc-spears (total: 8)\tMounted scouts of the Enemy can be found throughout the Entwash Vale. Thane Béortnoth asked you to hunt the mounted scouts of the Enemy and bring him their spears.\n2\tBring the Orc-spears to Thane Béortnoth outside of Thornhope\tThane Béortnoth is encamped beyond the walls of Thornhope. You should bring the spears you collected to Thane Béortnoth.\n",
[6322]="7000AC52\n1\tTalk to Soldier Kaasak at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect Rockwithers' horn\tRockwithers can be found among the Thistledown Grazers, south across the Hoarwell River. Angmar's forces at Tol Ascarnen are building a horn with which to call reinforcements to the fight when the Free Peoples return to assault the area. Kaasak has tasked you with retrieving the horn of the great aurochs, Rockwithers.\n",
[6323]="70067CB2\n1\tCollect sekbir-horns ([see journal]/12)\tHead into the wild lands of the Shield Isles and search for Ghar Jâdam, Sekbiri, or Bâkhabar jungle-beasts. Collect their horns ands return to Tanim at Halrax.\n2\tDeliver the jungle-beast horns to Tanim at Halrax\tYou slew several beasts in the Shield Isles and collected their horns. Tanim awaits your return at his home in Halrax.\n",
[6324]="7002EDFC\n1\tCollect metal fastenings from Rymenhild\030Collect pieces of leather (total: 5)\030Collect aurochs-ivory (total: 5)\tOffram has provided the ivory you need. Rymenhild can be found in the northern part of Eaworth. Leather can be found near the Vendor Hall in Eaworth. Offram wants you to collect the ivory, fastenings, and leather needed to craft battle-horns for the guards of Eaworth.\n2\tCraft battle-horns for the guards of Eaworth\tThe Quartermaster's workbench is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth. Offram asked you to take the materials you collect to the Quartermaster's workbench and craft battle-horns for the guards of Eaworth.\n3\tThe guards can be found throughout the city of Eaworth in the Entwash Vale. Offram asked you to deliver the battle-horns you crafted to the guards of Eaworth.\t\n4\tTalk to Offram outside the Vendor Hall in Eaworth\tOffram stands guard outside the Vendor Hall in Eaworth. You should let Offram know that you have delivered the battle-horns to the guards of Eaworth.\n",
[6325]="7002D506\n1\tCollect fresh hay (total: 8)\tThe hay-piles can be found around the stables and up the road towards Bree-town and Staddle.\n2\tReplace the horse's bedding\tThe horse-bedding can be found inside the horse's stall.\n",
[6326]="70028448\n1\tFind the missing horses\tThe horses were taken into the hills of western Nan Curunír. Dagoras asked you to find out where the stolen horses had been taken.\n2\tTalk to Ondor in Nan Curunír\tOndor is encamped near the caves of western Nan Curunír. You should tell Ondor that the goblins have been stealing horses and other livestock to feed the Wargs.\n",
[6327]="700076D2\n1\tTalk to Oddvarr\tThe old dwarf was last seen walking towards the old ruins to the south-east. Cam asked you to check up on an old dwarf who wanted to explore the ruins near Hengstacer.\n",
[6328]="7002C2ED\n1\tAsk Cynred if he will give you rations for your stay in Stangard\tCynred, the keeper of the food and keys, is near the lock-houses of Stangard in Eorlsmead. You should speak with Cynred at Sabert's recommendation that laws of hospitality be honoured.\n2\tTalk to Gadda, Lieutenant of Stangard, to gain entrance to the Mead Hall\tThe Mead Hall is the large structure at the top of Stangard's hill. You should seek entrance to the Mead Hall by speaking with Gadda, the guard.\n3\tTalk to Stanric, the captain at Stangard\tStanric, the leader of Stangard, can be found in the Mead Hall. You should seek hospitality in Stangard from Stanric.\n4\tSee what Sithric has to say\tSithric stands at the head of the Mead Hall in Stangard. You should speak with Sithric.\n",
[6329]="70047003\n1\tDeliver the bubbling goo to a collection box\030Collect bubbling goo (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire bubbling goo.\n",
[6330]="70047093\n1\tDeliver the burnt ears to a collection box\030Collect burnt ears (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire burnt ears.\n",
[6331]="70047002\n1\tDeliver the mouldy skins to a collection box\030Collect mouldy skins (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire mouldy skins.\n",
[6332]="70046FFE\n1\tDeliver the prismatic carapaces to a collection box\030Collect prismatic carapaces (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire prismatic carapaces.\n",
[6333]="70046FFF\n1\tDeliver the reeking filth to a collection box\030Collect reeking filth (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire reeking filth.\n",
[6334]="70047004\n1\tDeliver the worn fur to a collection box\030Collect worn furs (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire worn fur.\n",
[6335]="70037C8C\n1\tBreak the prisoners' chains to free them\tPrisoners can be found in Lufût-mos, the Uruk-encampment overlooking the Fords of Isen. You should break the chains of the prisoners at the Fords to free them.\n2\tBreak the prisoners' chains to free them (total: 5)\tPrisoners can be found in Lufût-mos, the Uruk-encampment overlooking the Fords of Isen. You should break the chains of the prisoners at the Fords to free them.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have freed a number of soldiers from their bonds at Lufût-mos. Their outlooks are much brighter, thanks to your heroic intervention.\n",
[6336]="700529E2\n1\tFind Hrában\030Find Skádda\030Find Grymil\tAinhard's three hounds, Hrában, Skádda, and Grymil, can be found somewhere in the forest near his home. You should find Hrában, Skádda, and Grymil and send them home.\n2\tTalk to Ainhard\tThe forester Ainhard lives south of Vegbár. You should talk to Ainhard.\n",
})
